    "message": "fix(mcp): register the resolved ix launcher on Windows\n\n`ix mcp install` wrote `command: \"ix\"` into all seven hosts. npm ships no\n`ix.exe` — only `ix.CMD` — and a host that spawns the bare name through\nCreateProcess never consults PATHEXT, so the registration resolves to\nnothing on Windows however well-formed the rest of it is.\n\nix-codex-plugin already hit this and resolves the path itself before\nspawning (its #13). Consolidating onto `ix mcp` would have discarded that\nfix and handed the same problem to every host, so the launcher is resolved\nonce here and each host records what `where ix` returned. Unix keeps the\nbare name, which survives an upgrade that moves the install.\n\nUntested on Windows from this machine; the Unix path is unchanged and\nresolution falls back to the bare name.",
